
Short Brief
👉 The code finds the first index where needle appears in haystack by checking every possible starting position and comparing characters one by one. If a full match is found, it returns the index; otherwise, it returns -1.

✅ Key Idea
👉 Compare the small string (needle) at every position in the big string (haystack).

✅ Complexities


Time Complexity: O(n × m)
👉 In the worst case, compare m characters for each of the n positions


Space Complexity: O(1)
👉 No extra space used


-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

class Solution {
    public int strStr(String haystack, String needle) {
        int n= haystack.length();
        int m= needle.length();

        for(int i=0;i<=n-m;i++){
            int j;
            for(j=0;j<m;j++){
                if(haystack.charAt(i+j)!=needle.charAt(j)){
                    break;
                }
            }
            if(j==m){
                return i;
            }
        }
        return -1;
        
    }
}
